<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Poro</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Poro society</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Poro is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> for men among peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a>, Liberia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Côte d'Ivoire</a>, including the Mende, Temne, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kpelle-people">Kpelle</a> and Vai. It initiates boys into adulthood through training in bush camps and has long held religious, political and judicial authority, regulating trade and warfare and helping to install chiefs. Its counterpart for women is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sande-society">Sande society</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/poro.jpg" alt="Poro" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sjoerd Hofstra · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SierraLeone_Hofstra_374.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
